      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1oqwzyo'
    '|a||Targets in quantities: tonnes of steel, metres of cloth, numbers of tractors. Prices were set too, but mostly to keep the books.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:x3mjep'
    '|b||Then how did the planners know there would be enough steel for all those tractors?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:kpnmbo'
    '|a||With a balance for each good: the steel to be made has to match the steel that everyone''s targets need.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:n26pne'
    '|a||In 1973 Gosplan itself balanced only about two thousand of the most important goods, in an economy that made millions of different products.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ado0ln'
    '|a||Try it, with illustrative numbers: raise the tractor target, and watch how much more steel, and then coal, the plan suddenly needs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1c6va4f'
    '|b||One target moves, and every balance upstream has to be redone. Largely by hand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Clumsy. And yet, for forcing growth, a plan is a powerful tool. It can decide to save: hold consumption down and pour output into steel mills, dams and power stations.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ml27ib'
    '|b||And it can move millions of peasants off the farms into factories, where each worker produces far more.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:dwq5s4'
    '|a||That''s the fast half: a plan is very good at doing a few big, obvious things, all at once.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:133me0s'
    '|b||Want the arithmetic behind those balances? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:gweqds'
    '|a||Each tonne of steel takes some steel to make: in the mills, the rails, the machines. Say a fifth of a tonne.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So to deliver d tonnes, the plan must make x equals d plus a fifth of x.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:m17py2'
    '|a||That''s d divided by 0.8: a quarter more than the final need. Wassily Leontief built thousands of such rows into one input–output table.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:orqg9m'
    '|a||A plan is good at big, obvious things. So what happened once the obvious things were built?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Here''s the slowdown: about three and a half percent a year in the fifties and sixties, under one and a half in the seventies and eighties.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:2e1ar3'
    '|a||Look inside one factory. Say Harbourtown''s boatyard runs under a plan, with illustrative numbers: a target of twenty boats, though it could build thirty.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1s4u5yz'
    '|b||You run the boatyard. Next year''s target will be this year''s output, plus a bit. How many boats do you build?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:nempc3'
    '|b||Many managers aimed just over the target, and kept the rest quiet.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Beat the target by a lot, and next year''s plan demands the lot. Economists call it the ratchet: so managers hid what they could really do.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And whatever the target doesn''t count, like quality or what buyers actually want, gets skimped.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:wuxazk'
    '|a||Meanwhile prices, fixed by planners, couldn''t say what was scarce: hence the queues and bare shelves of the shortage economy János Kornai described.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:2hadry'
    '|b||But those faults were there in the fifties, when growth was fast. Why did it slow only later?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ojn29f'
    '|a||William Easterly and Stanley Fischer''s answer: Soviet growth came mostly from piling up machines, and each extra machine added less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1gmqs3w'
    '|b||Market economies pile up machines too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1tnalm4'
    '|a||They do, but they keep finding good uses for the extra machines. The Soviet economy was unusually bad at that, so its returns fell faster.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:180ixwp'
    '|a||Robert Allen, though, blames choices more than the system: huge arms spending and wasteful investment that a better plan could have avoided.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1yn7y3j'
    '|a||So the incentives were poor, and the easy growth ran out. Is that the whole verdict?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Not even close. Take life expectancy in Russia: in 1928, thirty-nine years. America''s was fifty-eight.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1be777d'
    '|a||By 1960, sixty-eight against seventy. Almost the whole gap closed in a generation, helped by medicine the whole world got.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:wpkth5'
    '|b||Schooling too. In 1897 about a quarter of the people could read, by 1926 about half, by the 1950s nearly everyone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:kx8dda'
    '|a||And in 1957 the first satellite in orbit, Sputnik, was Soviet. Aim a whole country at a few goals, and it can hit them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:11y0y2d'
    '|b||Then the same stall: Russian life expectancy stuck near sixty-eight for twenty-five years, while America''s kept rising.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kto4ga'
    '|a||And the costs were enormous. Forced collectivisation of the farms was a major cause of the famine of 1930 to 1933, which killed an estimated 5.7 to 8.7 million people.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1mjzfw'
    '|b||And did it take a plan at all? Japan was about as poor in 1913, and by 1975 it had reached seventy percent of America''s income, without one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:10gzfq0'
    '|a||How sure are we? That the plan built industry, schools and health fast, at a terrible human cost: consensus.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:dckvlx'
    '|b||Why it stalled, and whether markets could have done as well with less suffering: still contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1q2bhd1'
    '|a||So planning could hit a few huge targets, and kept missing the millions of small ones that keep an economy growing.':
